<title>UK: S.Elec loses FTSE place to Imperial.</title>
<headline>S.Elec loses FTSE place to Imperial.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK-based conglomerate Hanson Plc's newly demerged Imperial Tobacco Group unit will knock privatised electicity distributor Southern Electric out of London's top 100 blue chips, FT-SE International said on Monday.</p>
<p>Southern Electric would become a constituent of its larger FTSE Mid 250 Index from end of trade today, it added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
